51	    /**
52	     * Formats the stored E.164 {@code telephone} for humans: the {@code '+'} and country code, a
53	     * space, then the national digits grouped in threes (e.g. {@code +61412345678} -&gt;
54	     * {@code +61 412 345 678}). The country code is taken as {@code 61} (Australia) or {@code 1}
55	     * (NANP) when recognised, otherwise a single leading digit. Returns {@code null} when the
56	     * telephone is absent, and the value unchanged when it is not a {@code '+'}-prefixed E.164
57	     * number.
